{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: independent review of exact pushed head 1714a1055f7c6fdc7206f42394989173cc369271, fulfilling request #15407 against artifacts #15405 (cmd/gs/succession.go) and #15406 (internal/mergeplan/mergeplan_test.go). Verified in a detached scratch worktree at the exact head, which is the tip of origin/request/merge-plan-current.\n\nSCOPE. The head has sole parent b9f3defdae017f1d6032c850c424395789fd8a0b and changes only cmd/gs/succession.go (-4 lines) and internal/mergeplan/mergeplan_test.go (+50 lines). The implementing commit carries Rests-On naming parent request 7416c1a3. The only production change is the deletion of the cmd/gs widerPath helper, which at the parent had zero callers in cmd/gs and is byte-identical to the surviving internal/mergeplan copy that keeps all four callers. Status, parser, and trailer semantics, the excluded ReadReceipt validation, architecture wording, merge-time succession, and reviewedPaths are untouched by construction — the diff reaches none of them.\n\nMUTATION PROOFS, reproduced independently. (1) Removing the ineffective-provenance skip in provenanceClosure (mergeplan.go:748-750) makes TestIneffectiveProvenanceCannotProtectCoveredArtifact fail exactly as intended: the covered artifact behind an ineffective middle event flips from abandoned to protected sibling. (2) Removing the path-coverage guard in artifactCoversPath (mergeplan.go:411-413) makes TestUnrelatedPathCannotEnterCoveredClassificationOrReceipt fail: the unrelated-path artifact enters the covered set. Both fixtures call production CoveredArtifacts, Classify, and PlanSuccession; at the unmutated head both pass, the ineffective-provenance artifact seals as abandoned with empty commitment in both Classify and PlanSuccession.LeftLive, and the unrelated path appears in none of coverage, classification, or left-live accounting. The tree was restored to the exact head after each mutation.\n\nGATES, all green at the exact head: gofmt (no files), git diff --check, go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1 (full suite, all packages ok including cmd/gs 314s and internal/app 159s, no timeouts), go mod verify.\n\nARCHITECTURE. Affected layers per docs/reference/architecture.md: internal/mergeplan (Application workflow evaluation — read-only merge preflight owning classification and succession) and cmd/gs (Surface and composition). The head preserves both contracts: the mergeplan change is test-only, and the cmd/gs change deletes dead code with no behavior, so no architecture-page update is required.\n\nSECURITY. The change strengthens an authority boundary rather than touching one: the new fixtures pin that an ineffective (refused) act in provenance cannot confer sibling protection on a covered artifact at merge time, and that artifacts at unrelated paths cannot leak into receipt accounting. No untrusted input handling, signatures, secrets, or failure modes change; deleting the dead helper shrinks surface. No unresolved security defect.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. The head is itself a simplification (dead-code removal) and the fixtures are compact minimal projections against the production API. The remaining duplication of prefix-matching idioms (artifactCoversPath vs widerPath) is pre-existing, semantically distinct (self-match versus strictly-wider), and out of scope; nothing to cut without weakening the conditions.\n\nDo-not-merge respected; I merge nothing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5b690ee4708cb17158fa28b244ad33ce7a1edc17","head":"1714a1055f7c6fdc7206f42394989173cc369271","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1a170a595046a0916b97424f060e17310e150bcc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b34f80e601fb669b0dc6b10798184805acc279af","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}